  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_8d251b64294e4d159847ca43912d4139",
      "statement": "The URL tenant segment is tenant *selection*, not authorization: a TenantScope is only ever built from the caller's own RLS-scoped memberships (`profile.tenants`), so `scopeForCode` returns null for a foreign code and the resulting `tenant_id = scope.tenantId` filter only picks among schools RLS already allows (RULES rule 2).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://RULES.md#L18-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c59217f5b544a8330dbf5d1c885e438f81b623fa8acd96de3c26b3258a94830:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://modules/tenancy/domain/scope.ts#L1-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e5380b0c562eb27cc2aa11177b7499ffb1b96f10b3747f63f8ff57e3aa53a30:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_befe919e9ffc4116a753bd50d487e7f4",
      "statement": "Before the URL segment existed, every office screen read every school the caller belonged to, so a multi-school user saw several schools' batches summed under one school's name (audit I1); a foreign code now never falls back to \"all schools\" but renders a not-available state with the caller's default school as a link, keeping the scoped URL shareable per ADR-001 K1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/(dashboard)/t/%5BtenantCode%5D/layout.tsx#L40-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2bab0f21132768697d5f1b5c4ee91073199740e37dbb712c44e829b1277d6721:"
        },
        {
